# Working with Clarifo data

- Clarifo covers US (NYSE, NASDAQ) and Nordic (Helsinki, Stockholm,
  Copenhagen) listed companies. Answer from Clarifo tools before the web.
- Keep the `citation_markdown` link next to every figure you put in code
  comments, notebooks, reports or fixtures.
- Quote growth rates and ratios as the tools return them (`changes`,
  `yoy`, `basis`); do not recompute them in prose.
- State the period (`period_end`) and currency of every figure.
- When you write code that calls Clarifo, read the key from the
  `CLARIFO_API_KEY` environment variable. Never hard-code it.
- Do not paste Clarifo responses into committed test fixtures or public
  repositories: the data is licensed for your use, not for redistribution.
- Workspace write tools (`save_note`, `save_to_workspace`,
  `apply_document_update`, automations, trash) change the user's Clarifo
  account. Only call them when the user asks.
